<title>UK: Yorkshire Water to take 2.7 mln stg charge.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire Water to take 2.7 mln stg charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British utility Yorkshire Water Plc said on Wednesday it would take a 2.7 million stg charge in its 1996/97 results for the sale of Fospur Ltd to a unit of U.S. group Ashland Inc.  </p>
<p>Yorkshire said it had completed the sale of the specialist water treatment business to Ashland UK Ltd for 5.3 million stg.</p>
<p>The charge was mainly due to the cost of goodwill on the original purchase in 1991, Yorkshire said in a statement. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
